### Type 2: C — Conventional

**What this type typically values:**

The Conventional type typically values organization, structure, accuracy and working with information or data. People with this interest often enjoy organizing information, following processes and completing tasks that require attention to detail.

**How this shows up in my life:**

This result makes sense because organization is one of the strengths I identified in my SWOT Analysis. My current job also requires me to work with data and information while managing different responsibilities and communicating across teams. Balancing a full-time career with school also requires me to stay organized and manage my time.

**Careers associated with this type that interest me:**

1. Financial Risk Specialist
2. Management Analyst
3. Financial & Investment Analyst

---

### Type 3: I — Investigative

**What this type typically values:**

The Investigative type typically values problem-solving, analyzing information, learning and understanding how things work. People with this interest often enjoy researching problems, working with information and using critical thinking to find solutions.

**How this shows up in my life:**

This type connects strongly with my interest in Data Science and cybersecurity. In my SWOT Analysis, I identified analyzing situations and finding solutions as one of my strengths. I also enjoy solving problems and developing new skills. My interest in gaining more hands-on Data Science experience and improving my technical skills also connects with the Investigative type.

**Careers associated with this type that interest me:**

1. Fraud Examiner, Investigator & Analyst
2. Financial Risk Specialist
3. Management Analyst

