## Connection to My Module 2 Findings

### Where my Holland Code and Module 2 findings align

My holland code aligns with the strengths and interest I identified in Module 2. My enterprising score shows a connection with my communication and networking skills as well as the desire to advance my career. I also understand why my conventional score was high as organization was one of my key strengths and I am also used to working with data and managing responsibilities in my current job. Investigative connects my problem-solving skills with my interest in Data Science and Cybersecurity. In my SWOT Analysis, I mentioned gaining hands on experience in Data Science and improving my technical skills as areas I would like to continue growing in.

### Where there are surprises or tensions

The biggest surprise to me was that Enterprising and Conventional were my two highest scores rather than Investigative. I expected Investigative to be my highest result as I am majoring in Data Science and have become very interested in Cybersecurity. However, after reviewing the careers that matched my results, I understood the scores better and they made sense. Many of the careers combined with business, technology and analysis which are areas that connect with my current career and my future career goals. I was also surprised to see management and analyst positions listed as some of my best career matches.

### What this tells me about my career direction

Combining my RIASEC results with my Module 2 findings showed my that I am possibly best suited for a career that combines my technical and analytical skills while also leveraging my current business experience. I do not think my results show that I need to change my Data Science major, but I think they do show that my strengths in communication, organization and problem solving are aligned with strengths needed in a technical career. This also supports my interest in exploring Cybersecurity. I don’t think I need to decide on one specific career, but these results allow me to find careers that combine my strengths and technical skills I am growing.
